<p>Here is how the law views your &quot;intentional&quot; argument:</p>
<h3>1. The Legal Obligation to Honor Prices</h3>
<p>Under Massachusetts Law <strong>940 CMR 5.02(6)</strong>, it is considered an <strong>unfair or deceptive act</strong> for a motor vehicle dealer to &quot;fail or refuse to sell a motor vehicle in accordance with any terms or conditions, including price... which the dealer has advertised&quot;.</p>
