<p><strong>Search&#39;s response:</strong><br>
To become the Mayor of Weymouth, Massachusetts, you must navigate a non-partisan election process governed by the <a href="https://ecode360.com/30092508">Weymouth Town Charter</a>. The Mayor serves as the town&#39;s chief executive for a four-year term.</p>
<h3>1. Confirm Eligibility</h3>
<p>Before running, ensure you meet the basic legal requirements:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Voter Registration:</strong> You must be a registered voter in Weymouth.</li>
<li><strong>Age:</strong> You must be at least 18 years old.</li>
<li><strong>Citizenship:</strong> You must be a U.S. citizen.</li>
<li><strong>Residency:</strong> You must be a resident of the Town of Weymouth.</li>
</ul>
<h3>2. File Your Intent</h3>
<p>Before gathering signatures, you must file a statement of candidacy with the <a href="https://www.weymouth.ma.us/town-clerk">Town Clerk&#39;s Office</a> at Town Hall (75 Middle Street). This statement includes your name, address, and the office you are seeking.</p>
<h3>3. Collect Nomination Signatures</h3>
<p>To appear on the ballot, you must gather certified signatures from registered Weymouth voters.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Total Required:</strong> At least <strong>150 certified signatures</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>District Requirement:</strong> You must obtain at least <strong>25 signatures from each</strong> of the town&#39;s six districts.</li>
<li><strong>Deadlines:</strong> Nomination papers are typically available starting in June of an election year and must be returned to the Board of Registrars for certification by late July.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4. Manage Campaign Finances</h3>
<p>You are required by law to track and report all campaign contributions and expenditures.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Registration:</strong> Register your campaign committee with the <a href="https://www.ocpf.us/">Office of Campaign and Political Finance (OCPF)</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Reporting:</strong> File regular financial disclosure reports according to the <a href="https://www.weymouth.ma.us/DocumentCenter/View/765/Local-Election-Schedule-2025">Local Election Schedule</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>5. Compete in the Elections</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Preliminary Election:</strong> Held on the third Tuesday in September if more than two candidates file for the office. The top two vote-getters advance to the general election.</li>
<li><strong>General Election:</strong> Held on the first Tuesday after the first Monday in November of odd-numbered years (e.g., 2025, 2029).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Summary of Key Dates (Based on 2025 Cycle)</h3>





























