<h3>Authenticity and Quality Tests</h3>
<p>Because saffron is frequently adulterated with safflower or dyed corn silk, use these tests to ensure you have a genuine product.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cold Water Test:</strong> Place a few threads in room temperature water. Real saffron will slowly release a yellowish-gold hue over several minutes. Fake saffron often releases a dark red or orange color almost immediately.</li>
<li><strong>Thread Appearance:</strong> Genuine threads are trumpet-shaped—fatter at the top and skinny at the bottom.</li>
<li><strong>Scent and Taste:</strong> Real saffron smells sweet (like honey and hay) but tastes slightly bitter. If it tastes sweet, it is likely fake.</li>
<li><strong>The Finger Rub:</strong> Rub the soaked threads between your fingers. Real threads will stay intact and stain your skin yellow or orange; fakes will often fall apart or stain red.</li>
</ul>
