<li><strong>Casing Ingredients</strong>: Common tobacco additives like <strong>licorice</strong> or certain sugars can sometimes produce a warm, spicy aroma when burned that mimics the scent of cloves.</li>
<li><strong>Freshness</strong>: Reviewers often note that 83s can taste &quot;fresher&quot; or more &quot;bold&quot; than standard Reds, which may intensify these natural tobacco spice notes.</li>
