<li><strong>Oriental Tobacco Ratio:</strong> Both use the &quot;American Blend,&quot; but Southern Cuts use a higher concentration of <strong>Oriental (Turkish) tobacco</strong>. This leaf is naturally very aromatic and &quot;peppery&quot; compared to the earthy Burley or sweet Virginia used in standard Reds.</li>
<li><strong>The 83s &quot;Freshness&quot;:</strong> Because 83s are packed slightly differently and marketed as a &quot;premium&quot; cut of the Red blend, they often have a higher moisture content. This prevents the tobacco from burning too hot and preserves the <strong>volatile oils</strong> in the tobacco, which makes those spicy, herbal notes stand out more than they would in a dry, dusty King Size Red.</li>
