<li><strong>Filter Efficiency</strong>: The longer filter on the 100s actually traps more of the nicotine and tar, leading to a <strong>lower yield</strong> (around 0.9 mg) compared to the shorter 83s (around 1.1 mg). This is likely why the 83s taste stronger and more consistent to you—you&#39;re getting more of the actual tobacco &quot;hit&quot; rather than it getting stuck in the filter.</li>
</ul>
<p>So, while the 100s technically have a few more milligrams of leaf, the <strong>83s</strong> deliver more of that weight directly to you because they aren&#39;t &quot;choked&quot; by a long filter.</p>
