In the United States, a citizen who discovers a stockpile of illegal weapons or explosives has a clear pathway—and in some specific legal contexts, an obligation—to report it to the authorities.</p>
<h3><strong>1. Legal Obligations and Risks</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Misprision of Felony</strong>: Under federal law (<a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/18/4">18 U.S. Code § 4</a>), if you have knowledge of a federal felony (like stockpiling illegal explosives) and you <strong>actively conceal</strong> it—such as by lying to investigators or hiding evidence—you can be charged with a crime punishable by up to three years in prison.</li>
<li><strong>Accessory After the Fact</strong>: If you assist those stockpiling the weapons in avoiding detection or capture, you can be prosecuted as an <a href="https://www.ronaldbrower.com/blog/2025/02/failure-to-report-a-crime-california/">accessory after the fact</a>.</li>
<li><strong>General Citizen Duty</strong>: While private citizens typically do not have a universal &quot;duty to report&quot; every crime, the <a href="https://www.atf.gov/explosives/tools-services-explosives-industry/current-licensees/suspicious-or-dangerous-items">ATF</a> strongly advises that anyone with knowledge of suspicious explosives-related activities report them immediately to protect public safety.</li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>2. How to Report Safely and Legally</strong></h3>
<p>If you have &quot;legitimate access&quot; and see a stockpile, the most effective and legal action is to contact professional agencies who have the equipment to handle explosives safely:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>ATF Tip Line</strong>: For illegal bombs or firearms, call <strong>1-888-ATF-BOMB</strong> (1-888-283-2662) or <strong>1-888-ATF-TIPS</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>FBI Tips</strong>: You can submit information online at <a href="https://tips.fbi.gov/">tips.fbi.gov</a> or contact a <a href="https://www.fbi.gov/contact-us/field-offices">local FBI field office</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Anonymity</strong>: You can report these tips anonymously to avoid direct confrontation or retaliation.</li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>3. Why Reporting is Better than &quot;Chaotic&quot; Intervention</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Evidence Integrity</strong>: Amateur intervention often destroys the &quot;chain of custody&quot; for evidence, making it impossible for prosecutors to actually convict the criminals.</li>
<li><strong>Public Safety</strong>: Handling improvised explosive devices (IEDs) without training is extremely dangerous. Professional bomb squads use specialized robots and containment units.</li>
<li><strong>Avoiding Counter-Charges</strong>: If a citizen enters a building forcefully or &quot;seizes&quot; items without a warrant, they can be charged with <strong>armed robbery</strong> or <strong>burglary</strong>, even if their intent was to help.</li>
