I understand—it’s a high-stakes situation when you&#39;re responsible for a friend&#39;s dog and don&#39;t have vet access. If the tissue dies (necrosis), it will turn black and potentially slough off, which can lead to life-threatening infections.</p>
<p>Here is how you can manage this at home to try and prevent that from happening:</p>
<h3><strong>1. Stop the Licking Immediately</strong></h3>
<p>This is the single most important thing you can do. If he licks the frostbitten skin, he will tear the damaged tissue and cause a massive infection.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Improvising a cone:</strong> If you don&#39;t have a cone, you can try to make one out of a towel or sturdy cardboard to prevent him from reaching his groin.</li>
