If the numbers can be repeated and the target number changes randomly after every incorrect guess, it is <strong>impossible to guarantee</strong> a correct answer in any fixed number of tries.</p>
<p>Because the &quot;correct&quot; number can be any of the 10 values every single time, you could theoretically guess wrong forever. Unlike a scenario where wrong answers are removed, these trials are independent, meaning your odds remain exactly <strong>1 in 10</strong> for every guess you make.</p>
<h3>Key Probability Facts for 2026:</h3>
