<li><strong>The &quot;Losing Streak&quot; Effect:</strong> In 100 trials, it is mathematically common to go 20 or 30 guesses without a single win.</li>
<li><strong>Expected Value:</strong> To &quot;guarantee&quot; a win, you would need an infinite number of trials, but for 100 trials, the most likely outcome is exactly 10 successes.</li>
</ul>
