<table><thead><tr><th align="left">If you want to find...</th><th align="left">Use this number...</th><th align="left">Logic</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left"><strong>Probability of a total failure streak</strong></td><td align="left">$0.9$ (Wrong)</td><td align="left">You must fail every single time.</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><strong>Probability of a perfect winning streak</strong></td><td align="left">$0.1$ (Right)</td><td align="left">You must succeed every single time.</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><strong>Probability of at least one win</strong></td><td align="left">$1 - (0.9)^n$</td><td align="left">$100%$ minus the chance of failing every time.</td></tr></tbody></table>
