<h3>The Caveats (Why it&#39;s still hard)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Risk of Defaults:</strong> Low-volume markets have higher volatility and higher risk of the asset becoming worthless (delisting risk). Your AI agent needs strong risk management.</li>
<li><strong>Slippage:</strong> You are more likely to encounter slippage (getting a worse price than expected when you execute the trade) in these markets.</li>
<li><strong>Execution Risk:</strong> You are relying on a homemade system on an old PC. Technical failures are a constant threat to your capital.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>In summary:</strong> The 4% goal is aggressive but achievable by trading where the big fish aren&#39;t swimming. Your scrappy, low-overhead setup is actually perfectly tailored for these specific, higher-margin opportunities.</p>
