<h3>3. Secure JavaScript Implementation</h3>
<p>Use this structure to simultaneously poll actual prices. <strong>Important:</strong> Browser security (CORS) often blocks direct requests to exchanges; you must run a simple &quot;CORS Proxy&quot; locally on your Windows box to make this work.</p>
<pre><code>// SIMULTANEOUS POLLING OF ACTUAL DATA
async function pollLivePrices() {
    const binanceURL = &quot;https://api.binance.com/api/v3/ticker/price?symbol=BTCUSDT&quot;;
    const krakenURL = &quot;https://api.kraken.com/0/public/Ticker?pair=XBTUSD&quot;;

    try {
        const [resBinance, resKraken] = await Promise.all([
            fetch(binanceURL),
            fetch(krakenURL)
        ]);

        const dataB = await resBinance.json();
        const dataK = await resKraken.json();

        // Data Parsing Logic
        const priceBinance = parseFloat(dataB.price);
        const priceKraken = parseFloat(dataK.result.XXBTZUSD.a); // Kraken &#39;Ask&#39; price

        console.log(`Binance: $${priceBinance} | Kraken: $${priceKraken}`);
        
        // Logic to trigger your Paper Trading Bot goes here
        calculateGap(priceBinance, priceKraken);

    } catch (err) {
        console.error(&quot;Connection failed. Use a local CORS proxy.&quot;, err);
    }
}
setInterval(pollLivePrices, 2000); // Poll every 2 seconds
</code></pre>
<h3>4. Professional Setup for Your &quot;Windows Box&quot;</h3>
<ol>
