In the context of a U-Haul rental dispute, a <strong>CAF</strong> stands for <strong>Customer Action File</strong>. This is the primary internal process used to document and resolve customer complaints, including issues related to safety or damage.</p>
<h3>How Compensation is Handled via a CAF</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Initial Review:</strong> Once a CAF is created, it is assigned to the managers responsible for your rental location.</li>
<li><strong>Resolution Timeline:</strong> Managers typically have <strong>three days</strong> to address the issue. If they fail to do so in a timely manner, the file is automatically forwarded to the U-Haul corporate office for further action.</li>
<li><strong>Compensation Potential:</strong> While a CAF is primarily for documenting a dispute, it often leads to partial refunds or &quot;money back for your time&quot; if the manager finds the complaint valid.</li>
<li><strong>Return Process:</strong> Having the CAF already on file should streamline your return process, as the location manager will have access to the documented history of your safety concerns and contaminated belongings.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Important Considerations for Your Claim</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Ensure you have photographic evidence of any contamination or safety defects to present during the return.</li>
<li><strong>Insurance Coverage:</strong> Standard U-Haul cargo protection (like SafeMove) typically covers damage from accidents, fires, or windstorms, but may exclude &quot;mysterious disappearance&quot; or specific types of contamination. If you declined coverage, you may be limited to what you can negotiate directly with the manager for their negligence.</li>
<li><strong>Further Action:</strong> If the location manager cannot provide a satisfactory resolution, you can escalate the claim by calling <strong>1-800-GO-UHAUL</strong> or filing a formal <strong>Notice of Dispute</strong> to begin arbitration.</li>
</ul>
<p>For direct assistance or to check the status of your file, you can visit the <a href="https://www.uhaul.com/Contact/">U-Haul Contact Page</a> or call 1-800-468-4285.</p>
