<p><strong>Search&#39;s response:</strong><br>
In a medical context, &quot;Pt denies changes in NVS&quot; typically means the <strong>patient denies experiencing any changes related to their neurological vital signs</strong>.</p>
<p>Here&#39;s a breakdown:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pt:</strong> This is a common medical abbreviation for <strong>patient</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Denies:</strong> In medical documentation, &quot;denies&quot; means the patient reports that they are <em>not</em> experiencing a particular symptom or condition.</li>
<li><strong>NVS:</strong>  This abbreviation most commonly stands for <strong>neurological vital signs</strong>. This refers to assessments of a patient&#39;s neurological status, such as level of consciousness, pupillary response, and motor function.</li>
</ul>
<p>Therefore, &quot;Pt denies changes in NVS&quot; indicates that the patient has been asked about potential changes in their neurological vital signs and has stated that they have not noticed any changes. This information is important for tracking a patient&#39;s neurological health and identifying potential problems early.</p>
