<p><strong>Search&#39;s response:</strong><br>
A comprehensive metabolic panel (CMP) is a group of blood tests that provides an overview of your body&#39;s chemical balance and metabolism. It measures several substances in your blood, including:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Glucose:</strong>  70 - 100 mg/dL.</li>
<li><strong>BUN (Blood Urea Nitrogen):</strong> 6 - 19 mg/dL. The normal range can vary slightly depending on the lab, but a general range is 7 to 20 mg/dL. If the BUN level is higher than normal, it may be a sign of kidney problems, although it can also be influenced by dehydration or high protein intake.</li>
<li><strong>Creatinine:</strong> 0.4 - 1.2 mg/dL. Too much creatinine in the blood can indicate kidney issues.</li>
<li><strong>eGFR (Estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate):</strong> Above &gt;60.00 mL/min/1.73m*2. A normal eGFR is typically above 90, but it declines with age. An eGFR below 60 may indicate kidney disease.</li>
<li><strong>Sodium:</strong> 135 - 145 mmol/L. Normal range is 135 to 145 mEq/L.</li>
<li><strong>Potassium:</strong> 3.4 - 5.1 mmol/L. Normal range is between 3.7 and 5.2 mEq/L.</li>
<li><strong>Chloride:</strong> 98 - 109 mmol/L. Normal range is 96 to 106 mEq/L.</li>
<li><strong>CO2 (Carbon Dioxide):</strong> 24 - 32 mmol/L.  The normal range is typically 23 to 29 mEq/L. The CO2 blood test measures bicarbonate levels.</li>
<li><strong>Anion Gap:</strong> 6 - 12 mmol/L. Normal range is typically 8 to 12 mEq/L, but this can vary between laboratories.</li>
<li><strong>Calcium:</strong> 8.5 - 10.5 mg/dL. Normal range is 8.5 to 10.2 mg/dL.</li>
<li><strong>Total Bilirubin:</strong> 0.2 - 1.2 mg/dL. Normal range is 0.1 to 1.2 mg/dL.</li>
<li><strong>Alkaline Phosphatase:</strong> 40 - 129 U/L. Normal range is 20 to 130 U/L.</li>
<li><strong>ALT (SGPT):</strong> 0 - 40 U/L.  Normal range is typically about 7 to 56 U/L, but this can vary by laboratory.</li>
<li><strong>AST:</strong> 0 - 37 U/L. Normal ranges for adults vary slightly between males and females, generally ranging from 8 to 48 U/L.</li>
<li><strong>Total Protein:</strong> 6.0 - 8.5 g/dL. Normal range is 6.0 to 8.3 g/dL.</li>
<li><strong>Albumin:</strong> 3.3 - 5.2 g/dL. Normal range is 3.4 to 5.4 g/dL.</li>
<li><strong>Corrected Calcium:</strong> 8.5 - 10.5 mg/dL.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Important Note:</strong> The normal ranges provided in the initial comprehensive metabolic panel image you provided, as well as the normal ranges from the search results, can vary slightly between different laboratories. It is best to consult with your healthcare provider to understand the meaning of your specific test results.</p>
